{
  "id": "attunement",
  "term": "attunement",
  "definition": "In counselling ethics, attunement means a therapist’s sensitive, moment-to-moment awareness of the client’s needs, the purpose of what the therapist is doing, and the context of the therapeutic relationship. In this sense, ethical and effective decisions depend on staying closely responsive to these factors.",
